# Validity report

Generated by `sul validate` (PROJECT_SPEC.md §M6). A section marked **NOT
MEASURED OFFLINE** could not be evaluated against the provider that produced
it -- the reason is given in that section, and no number is printed in its
place. A section marked **PARTIALLY MEASURED** dispatched real calls but lost
one or more subjects to a mid-probe failure (PROJECT_SPEC.md §M6 Deviation
11); every number in it is computed only over the subjects that survived,
never padded to look like full-panel coverage -- the subject count next to
each such number is the denominator that number was actually computed over.
Provenance (provider, and model per agent role) is a field on every row
below, read back from the `ModelCall` audit trail for exactly the runs that
produced that row -- not one blanket value for the whole report, since a
mixed run can back different checks with different providers or models.

